<topic xml:id="reference-deployment-manual-product-selection"
 role="reference" xml:lang="en"
 xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2"
 xmlns:its="http://www.w3.org/2005/11/its"
 xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"
 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
 xmlns:trans="http://docbook.org/ns/transclusion">
  <info>
   <title>Selecting a product and installation mode</title>
    <meta name="maintainer" content="cwickert@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
    <abstract><!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
      <para>
       In this step, you select the product and its installation mode.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <figure xml:id="fig-deployment-manual-product-selection">
    <title>&agama; installer product selection</title>
    <mediaobject>
      <textobject role="description">
        <phrase>Screenshot of the &agama; installer showing the product selection. It allows for
          installing &slsa; and &sles4sapa; in standard or immutable mode.</phrase>
      </textobject>
      <imageobject role="fo">
        <imagedata fileref="agama-installation-sles-select-product.png" width="100%"/>
      </imageobject>
      <imageobject role="html">
        <imagedata fileref="agama-installation-sles-select-product.png" width="100%"/>
      </imageobject>
    </mediaobject>
  </figure>
  <para>
    Select &productname; &productnumber; for installation and choose its installation mode:
  </para>
  <variablelist>
    <title>Installation modes</title>
    <varlistentry>
      <term><guilabel>Standard</guilabel></term>
      <listitem>
        <para>
          The file system is writable. This mode offers maximum flexibility.
        </para>
      </listitem>
    </varlistentry>
    <varlistentry>
      <term><guilabel>Immutable</guilabel></term>
      <listitem>
        <para>
          The root file system is write-protected. Updates are applied
          atomically to a new snapshot. The snapshot becomes active after a reboot.
        </para>
      </listitem>
    </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
  <para>
    Read and accept the license to continue.
  </para>
  <tip>
    <title>Additional installer features</title>
    <para>
      At the top right of the installer, there is a tool bar with icons to access additional
      installer features:
    </para>
    <variablelist>
      <title>Icons (from left to right)</title>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Status icon</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Shows the status of the installer. <literal>Idle</literal> means the installer is
            waiting for input.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Language and keyboard icons</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Allows changing the language and keyboard layout of the installer. This affects only the
            installer interface, not the product to be installed. You can adjust the localization of
            the product later in <xref linkend="reference-deployment-manual-language-region"/>.
          </para>
          <!--
          <para>
            The keyboard layout can only be changed on local installations. If you are using a Web
            browser for a remote installation, configure the preferred content language in the
            browser settings and reload the installer.
          </para>
          -->
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Appearance icon</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Allows changing the color scheme and contrast of the installer.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>More</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Allows downloading the configuration in the JSON format and the installation logs.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
    
  </tip>
</topic>
